{
    "_comment": [
        "Per-window-kind layout for TP messages. The kind is the fuki_kind byte",
        "of each message's INF1 attributes (see window_kinds.py / TAGS.md).",
        "warn_width / max_width are line width limits in font px; null means",
        "'use the global plugin settings'. font_file picks the BFN font for the",
        "kind (empty = default font). lines_per_page drives preview pagination",
        "and the page-height scale. Explicit per-string overrides always win.",
        "An optional 'name' labels the kind in the editor (the preview badge and",
        "the Window: label). Unknown kinds show as 'Dialogue (kind N)' - to",
        "classify one (e.g. the ring-menu item info screen), add its number here",
        "with a name, widths and lines_per_page."
    ],
    "default": {
        "warn_width": null,
        "max_width": null,
        "font_file": "",
        "lines_per_page": 4
    },
